COMPENSATION ROUND ADVERSARY REPORT FOR LP_exc^rel

0. UPFRONT VERDICT

Verdict: PARTIAL.
1. Adversary breakthroughs inside H = O(x / T) [proved + measured]:
   - Unlike the dd round — where Codex's quadratic-pole family sent H -> infinity (experiments/dd/codex/proof.txt:105) and Gemini's C3 paid H >= Omega(D m^2 log m) (experiments/dd/gemini/proofs.txt:83) — twisting a boosted KH-floor divided-difference module by an Alon-Vu adjugate C* = g_0^{-1} adj(B_0) (Family M3_adjZ) or a unimodular O_k-staircase inverse B_{Ok}^{-1} (Family M4_uniOk) stays strictly inside H = O(x / T) while achieving certified loss lambda_i = log(M_i / t_i) >= (m/2) log m - O(m) at u = (1 - o(1)) D (resp. >= c m log m at D/2) embeddings (codex/scratch/dd_g/comp_proofs.txt:3-37). At 96 bits (n = 12, m = 3..6), H stays at 230..560 (6x below dd's 1150..3155) while median loss climbs 2.72 -> 4.24 -> 6.44 -> 7.43 (M3_adjZ) and 4.23 -> 4.92 -> 6.95 -> 8.36 (M4_uniOk) (codex/scratch/dd_g/comp_results.json:2190-3065).
   - Mixing linear and cyclotomic poles with unit remainders (Family M2_mix) produces up to 35 non-scalar capped candidates of exact norm |F| = 1 (log|F| = 0, far below the KH floor) whose union spans full k-rank m/m [proved + measured], refuting the literal wording "every non-scalar capped candidate has log|F| >= (1 - o(1))*(KH floor)" in codex/comp_common.md:13-14 unless "non-scalar" is replaced by "outside proper k-subspaces and unit products".
2. Failure to break LP_exc^rel and proved Compensation Obstructions [proved + measured]:
   - Across ALL 55 pre-registered main runs from 60 to 112 bits (five constructions, seeds 19 and 0, m = 3..5), parity-independent yield modulo proper k-subspaces and lower-norm products is N_ind = 0 in every single box (55/55 zeros, even at 60 and 72 bits!) (comp_results.json:1-2189).
   - Every one of the four prompt mechanisms hits a proved obstruction (Section 4): the Submodule-KH Compensation Lemma forces Q >= (1 - o(1)) x/T - O_k(Dm) whenever u = D - o(D) embeddings share a ternary basis; a two-place covolume bound forbids conjugate absorption over O_k; a Cramer Support-Width Lemma proves >= (gamma/e - o(1)) m poles must carry amplitude >= e^{lambda/2} (killing small-cluster pole splitting); and an exact general-pole divided-difference identity extends rho-inflation to arbitrary mixed/quadratic/cyclotomic poles.

All scratch files (comp_prereg.txt, run_comp_adversary.py, comp_proofs.txt, comp_results.json) are in /Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/dd_g; repository files are untouched.


1. PRE-REGISTERED ADVERSARIAL CONSTRUCTIONS IN H = O(x / T)

All five families were pre-registered in codex/scratch/dd_g/comp_prereg.txt:1-47 before running 60-112 bit benchmarks, over k = Q(sqrt(2)) (e = 2) on N = a^2 - 2 fixtures (experiments/subthird/codex/experiment.py:28-43, seeds 19 and 0), ternary box Omega = [-1, 1]^{2m}, ideal-relative cap |F|/J <= 3^{4n} 2^{ceil(bits/(2n))}, and B = 2^{ceil((bits * bit_length(bits-1)^3)^{1/4})} (codex/scratch/dd_g/run_comp_adversary.py:185-278):

1. M1_clust (Split pole clusters): Linear poles split across small clusters in {-2, -1, 1, 2, 3} with small graded integer remainders S(r_j) in P = S + R U, Q = P + j_0(T - b)R (centered base-b U of degree n - m + 2), testing whether distributing residues across clusters avoids Q-inflation.
2. M2_mix (Mixed linear + quadratic cyclotomic unit-circle poles): Poles [T - 1, T^2 + 1, T^2 + T + 1, T^2 - T + 1][:m-2] with roots on |z| = 1 and unit remainder S = 1 (P = 1 + R U). Because |zeta| = 1, |U(zeta)| <= n b avoids |r_j|^n pole blow-up while generating exact non-scalar units (alpha - 1), (P // (T-1))(alpha), and (P // (T^2+1))(alpha) of two-sided norm 1.
3. M3_adjZ (Alon-Vu adjugate twist w = C* v_tilde): Takes KH-floor poles R_j = T - (4 + j) (outside |z| <= 2) with S = 1, boosts generator 1 to c_1 = nextprime(4m + 2) coprime to N so v_tilde_1 dominates on |alpha_i| <= 2, and applies primitive C* = g_0^{-1} adj(B_0) in Z^{m x m} of an invertible ternary Z-matrix B_0 maximizing ||B_0^{-1}||_max (heavy column on c_1). Since ||adj(B_0)||_max <= (m-1)^{(m-1)/2}, achieving ||B_0^{-1}||_max = exp((m/2) log m - O(m)) tautologically forces |det B_0| <= exp(O(m)) [proved] (comp_proofs.txt:12-19), keeping H(w) = O(x / T) while B_0 w = +-Delta* v_tilde forces lambda_i >= (m/2) log m - O(m) at (1 - o(1)) D embeddings!
4. M4_uniOk (Unimodular O_k-staircase + Pell conjugate-absorption twist): Applies exact unimodular B_{Ok}^{-1} in GL_m(O_k) (where B_{Ok} has diagonal -1+sqrt(2) and subdiagonal -(1+sqrt(2)), det B_{Ok} = (-1+sqrt(2))^m in O_k^*, so J_w = J_v has zero determinant loss) multiplied by (-1+sqrt(2))^{2m-1} so M_i ~ O(m), t_i << 1 at sigma_1 (D/2 embeddings), testing whether compensating sigma_2 conjugates absorb Q.
5. M5_sunit (Per-side large-field unit-scaled Newton module + twist): Uses m - 1 unit-remainder poles P(r_l) = Q(r_l) = 1 so every (alpha - r_l, alpha' - r_l) and ((P // R_1)(alpha), (Q // R_1)(alpha')) is an exact linked unit in O_K^* x O_{K'}^*, forming unit basis (c_1 (P // R_1)(alpha), alpha - r_1, ..., prod_{l=1}^{m-1}(alpha - r_l)) twisted by B_{Ok}^{-1}.


2. CERTIFIED MEASUREMENTS AT 60-112 BITS

Generator ideal norms J = N(c)N(c') are computed exactly via PARI nfinit/idealadd/idealnorm; all thresholds M_i, t_i, H = sum log M_i - log J, and Q = sum log t_i - log J are certified with 512-bit flint arb/acb ball arithmetic; all norms and ideal parities use exact flint resultants and PARI idealprimedec (run_comp_adversary.py:283-501). Every box verified slow growth s_h <= h(p + 1) + 1.

