Why M2_mix had kRk = 4/4 yet N_ind = 0: Inspecting all 37 capped orbits at (112, 12, 4) shows every single capped vector has coordinate support in {(0,), (1,), (2,), (3,), (0,1), (0,2)} (proper k-subspaces of dimension <= 2 containing exact units 1, alpha-1, (P//(T-1))(alpha), (P//(T^2+1))(alpha) of norm 1 or 2^{24}); ZERO capped vectors have support size >= 3. In M1_clust, M3_adjZ, M4_uniOk, and M5_sunit, the entire capped set has k-rank <= m - 1 at 84-112 bits.


3. EXPONENT LEDGER

In src/grdeg/ledger.py:37-101 (d = x^delta, r = x^rho, log B = x^alpha, rho = alpha, alpha = 1/(4 - c) for N-saving exponent 1 + c*rho - delta) [proved arithmetic; heuristic endpoints]:
- M1_clust, M2_mix (untwisted small/unit remainders, p = Theta(m)): Outside proper k-subspaces, deg N_a = p + 1 >= m - 1 roots of modulus O(1) miss R = 0 and pay |F(a)| ~ b^{4(p+1)} >= N^{4(m-1)/(n-p)} => log|F| ~ (r/d) x, so c = 1, delta = 2/3, alpha = 1/3 (matching measured escaping ratios 1.79..2.70 at 84-112 bits).
- M3_adjZ, M4_uniOk, M5_sunit (basis-twisted modules w = C* v_tilde): Any ternary z in [-1,1]^{2m} outside ker_small(C*^T) maps to z_tilde = C*^T z of height exp(Theta(m log m)), paying log(|F|/J) >= (r/d) x + Theta(D m log m) (c >= 1, alpha >= 1/3; measured escaping ratios 3.69..4.23); vectors landing inside small-height subspaces of v_tilde inherit c = 1 above.


4. SHARPEST PROVED OBSTRUCTIONS (PARTIAL COMPENSATION LEMMA)

Complete proofs are in codex/scratch/dd_g/comp_proofs.txt:40-114:

1. Submodule-KH Compensation Lemma [proved] (comp_proofs.txt:42-69):
   For ANY reduced linked O_k-module M of rank m and ANY invertible ternary matrix B in A^{m x m}, the submodule M_B := B * M has k * M_B = k * M (hence identical KH degree T) and c_B subseteq c, so J_B = N(c_B)N(c'_B) >= J (log(J_B / J) >= 0 HELPS the bound). Applying Ideal-Relative Theorem KH (notes/subthird_results.md:136) to M_B gives sum_i log M_{B,i} - log J >= (x - D log(C_k D))/T. If B witnesses M_{B,i} <= e^{kappa_i} t_i on a set U_B of u embeddings while M_{B,j} <= C_k m e^{lambda_j} t_j on U_B^c, then
     Q >= (x - D log(C_k D)) / T - sum_{i in U_B} kappa_i - sum_{j notin U_B} lambda_j - (D - u) log(C_k m).
   In particular, whenever u = D - o(D) embeddings share B with kappa_i = O_k(m) (as in M3_adjZ), Cramer's bound lambda_j <= (e/2) m log m + O_k(m) on the o(D) exceptions gives Q >= (1 - o(1)) x/T - O_k(Dm) unconditionally! And when B in GL_m(O_k) is unimodular on u = D/2 embeddings (M4_uniOk), z |-> B^{-T} z preserves all proper k-subspaces and norms identically.

2. Two-Place Covolume Obstruction Against Conjugate Absorption [proved] (comp_proofs.txt:71-83):
   For any m k-independent vectors u^(1), ..., u^(m) in O_k^m (k = Q(sqrt(2))) and any two invertible ternary matrices B_1, B_2 in A^{m x m} with ||sigma_r(B_r) sigma_r(u^(l))||_inf <= tau_r (r = 1, 2), combining 1 <= |N_{k/Q}(det U)| with Hadamard |sigma_r(det B_r)| >= (C_k sqrt(m))^{-m} proves log tau_1 + log tau_2 >= -2 log(C_k m). Thus -m log m log-thresholds at sigma_1 MUST be paid back +m log m - O(log m) at sigma_2; conjugate absorption fails.

3. Support-Width Lemma & General-Pole Divided-Difference Identity [proved] (comp_proofs.txt:88-114):
   - Support-Width: Any y in C^m \ {0} with log(||y||_inf / ||sigma(A)y||_inf) = lambda >= gamma m log m has s_big := #{j : |y_j| >= e^{-lambda/2} ||y||_inf} >= (gamma/e - o(1)) m (by Cramer on an invertible s_big x s_big minor of sigma(A)_{J_big}), forbidding small-cluster localization of loss to o(m) poles.
   - General-Pole Identity: For ANY monic squarefree pole polynomial R_j(T) of degree d_j >= 1 with roots beta_{j,1..d_j} under sigma, Lagrange remainder interpolation yields identically
       w_{2+j}(alpha_i) = f_sigma[alpha_i, beta_{j,1}, ..., beta_{j,d_j}]
                        = sum_{nu=1}^{d_j} [ prod_{l != i} (beta_{j,nu} - alpha_l) ] / R'_{j,sigma}(beta_{j,nu}),
     unifying linear-pole rho-inflation (Gemini C3) and quadratic-pole B-inflation (Codex R_j = T^2 - r_j^2, dd/codex/proof.txt:49) across all Theta(m) heavy poles.


5. WHAT REMAINS AND NEXT STEP

What remains open in the Compensation Lemma: ONLY the fully non-aligned regime where u ~ D embeddings attain lambda_i ~ m log m using pairwise distinct, unshared ternary bases A^(i) (with max_B |U_B| = o(D)) inside H = O(x/T).
Concrete next step: Prove that on any degree-(p + 1) divided-difference numerator curve alpha |-> [G(alpha)] in P^{m-1}(C) with H = O(D m log m), at most O_{k,gamma}(m) non-clustered roots can land in distinct singular subspaces E_{A^(i)} (from dd/gemini/proofs.txt:101), forcing a single basis B to be shared by u = D - O(m + log b) = D - o(D) embeddings if u ~ D, where Theorem 4.1 (Submodule-KH) immediately closes Q >= (1 - o(1)) x/T.
